# Diagrams & resource efficiency

## Graphs / diagrams
- Use Mermaid for flows, sequences, ERDs, component trees; tables for comparisons.
- One diagram = one question. Label edges. No decorative nodes.
- Prefer: architecture context → sequence for runtime → state for modes.
- See `.cursor/guides/diagrams.md` for templates.

## Less resource, excellent output
- Batch independent tool calls; don’t re-read files you already have.
- Search narrowly (`rg`/glob) before wide exploration.
- Edit surgically; don’t regenerate whole files for small diffs.
- Depth only on the critical path; skip optional polish unless asked.
- Cache decisions in the plan; don’t re-derive architecture mid-task.
- Prefer reuse of existing components/tokens over new abstractions.
